    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWithout multicursor, the undolist isn't updated when entering and exiting insert mode, provided that no changes were actually made to the buffer. However, with multiple cursors placed, typing `i<esc>` causes the undolist to be updated.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean\n:undolist\n# observe the message \"Nothing to undo\"\ni<Esc>\n:undolist\n# observe that it still displays \"Nothing to undo\"\nQ\ni<Esc>\n:undolist\n# observe that the undolist now has an entry\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nJust like with a single cursor, the undolist would only be modified if the buffer text actually changed.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0, a6d91a8d7c1bcce43e3ce96955b9120ff0a21cf5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno (no multicursor)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS unstable\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nnixpkgs",
